CIRA-WM compact public companion, 2026-10-27.

Selected research method modules are copied without modification from
D-Star-Robotics/CIRA-WM commit e5312d488c8034be940bc3fc82586e1f25eb4c3a.
SOURCE_MANIFEST.json records their original source paths and content identities.
The existing repository license text is retained in LICENSE.

CIRA-WM builds on NVIDIA PointWorld:
https://github.com/NVlabs/PointWorld

This compact companion does not redistribute the full PointWorld backbone,
PTv3 implementation, DINOv3 code, pretrained weights or raw third-party datasets.
Those components retain their own upstream copyright and license terms.

Three rendered BEHAVIOR colored-point-cloud excerpts and posters are included.
Source annotations: NVIDIA PointWorld-BEHAVIOR, derived from BEHAVIOR.
Dataset reference: https://huggingface.co/datasets/nvidia/PointWorld-BEHAVIOR
Original project: https://behavior.stanford.edu/
These excerpts replay recorded ground-truth geometry; they are not CIRA
prediction comparisons, continuous model rollouts or task-success evidence.
Source-data and asset terms remain applicable to media. The repository code
license does not replace those terms or grant a new license to source datasets.
No ownership of external robot assets or upstream world models is claimed.
